{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1538688-could-wraiths-be-fake","id":1538688,"title":"Could Wraiths be Fake?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-16T18:53:02-07:00","id":1538688,"title":"Could Wraiths be Fake?","content":"Let's try some imagination: <br /> Now, we know that some items destroyed in the Material World can end up &quot;appearing&quot; in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> But... Is that really true?<br /> <br /> Stuff in the Underworld are not really made of carbon and silicon... They are made of Corpus.<br /> <br /> And what is &quot;Corpus&quot;? It is some weird &quot;spiritual&quot; stuff.<br /> <br /> We also know that stuff in this plane of existence are highly affected by emotions... Memories, emotions, all of that shape the environment and even it's inhabitants.<br /> <br /> The Corpus of the Wraiths itself is highly dependant on their emotions - a Wraith that has no more passions simply ceases to be, their very &quot;Corpus&quot; dissipates into nothingness.<br /> <br /> Therefore, this is a Realm of pure emotion... It is an abstract Realm of thought.<br /> <br /> In that sense... It might not even be real! It could just be a &quot;theater of the mind&quot; for all we know. A sort of &quot;collective acid trip&quot;.<br /> <br /> But that's not the point. The point is that Wraiths may not be &quot;souls&quot;, but just simply a &quot;mental reflection&quot; of the deceased!<br /> <br /> This is a Realm that could copy the minds of those that died with far too strong will - so, if your will is too strong, it will &quot;imprint&quot; your mind into this Realm.<br /> <br /> But it is NOT &quot;you&quot;, but a mental copy of what you once were.<br /> <br /> There's actually some indication that this might be true. First of all, everything points out to there being a difference between &quot;soul&quot; and &quot;mind&quot;. Proof of that is that you actually need Spirit 5 in order to create a real human being, rather than just Mind 5.<br /> <br /> Secondly, there's indication that &quot;souls&quot; mostly don't carry over details of the &quot;mind&quot;, except for few fragments, with a few exceptions. How do we know this? Because Mage actually has reincarnation, and almost all of the time save very rare exceptions, you NEVER get details from &quot;past minds&quot; except for some disconnected flashes.<br /> <br /> Therefore, Mind (memory and emotions) is NOT the same as &quot;Soul&quot; (whatever that might be).<br /> <br /> The thing is thou, that Wraiths keep their full Minds upon their &quot;transition&quot;. They remain essentially the SAME as they &quot;were&quot; when alive, the same memories, the same psychology, the same emotions (sure, colourful due to their environment).<br /> <br /> Reincarnated Mages on the other hand, are different persons from their previous lives (different memories, different experiences, different minds)<br /> <br /> That is a strong indication that Wraiths are the &quot;Mind&quot; of the dead, rather than their &quot;Soul&quot;.<br /> <br /> The other problem we have relate to &quot;Avatars&quot;.<br /> <br /> What is an Avatar you might ask?<br /> <br /> I have no freaking idea, but but there's a strong implication that &quot;Avatars&quot; have something to do with &quot;Souls&quot;, whatever a &quot;Soul&quot; is either.<br /> <br /> And while I might not know what a Wraith is... I'm sure as hell that they aren't Avatars (from Mage)<br /> <br /> Therefore, I believe that there's a strong possibility that Wraiths aren't really souls, but rather just &quot;psychic reflections&quot; of the living upon the dreadful Underworld... As in, this is a Realm that &quot;copy&quot; the minds of strong willed individuals.<br /> <br /> That would make Wraiths be something akin to the Chimeras from the Dreaming. The Spirits of the Dreaming, the Chimeras, they are &quot;born&quot; out of the dreams and imagination of the dreamers (or sleepers or just simply &quot;humans&quot;). Wraiths could then, be something similar<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T04:24:57-07:00","id":1538725,"title":"","content":"I think it is a bit problematic to look at the question from the perspective of another system, and I disagree with the idea that a Wraith is merely a memory gestalt. If you would ask me for a game mechanic definition of what a Wraith is, I would answer something along the line of &quot;an ephemeral entity expressing the soul of deceased person&quot;. I think the misunderstanding is casually referring to Wraiths and Souls interchangeably in a prosaic way. The rules in WtO clearly make a distinction between the two, though.<br /> <br /> A Wraith <i>has </i>a soul, rather than <i>being </i>a soul. The Corpus, Shadow and Psyche, Fetters and Passions are merely parts of the expression that define a Wraith as an entity in the Underworld, much like a physical body and mind does for a person in the Skinlands. Even removing some of these aspects does not erase the soul of the Wraith, only Oblivion does (at least until you get to a Ship of Theseus situation).<br /> <br /> The rules in all systems deliberately avoid making a definition of what a soul is, even if there are mechanics that directly affect it (ie diablerie in VtM or some Arcanoi in WtO). Soul remains an abstract concept, and in the most rudimentary sense it means the Thing That Makes You You. There is nothing stopping a Mage character from assuming your idea, but it does conflict with the rules as presented in WtO itself.<br /> <br /> As for Avatars, I personally treat them as separate entities that merge with a Mage's soul. Perhaps as something like a colloid rather than a solution, but that's probably something for the Mage forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T07:36:04-07:00","id":1538746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1538688-could-wraiths-be-fake?p=1538725#post1538725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for Avatars, I personally treat them as separate entities that merge with a Mage's soul. Perhaps as something like a colloid rather than a solution, but that's probably something for the Mage forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting perspective. It could give room for the Technocratic idea that Avatars are &quot;alien parasites&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thank you for the answer. I gotta say thou, this idea of Wraiths as forgeries has fascinated me, even thou I know it's probably not the case","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T10:33:28-07:00","id":1538768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1538688-could-wraiths-be-fake#post1538688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's try some imagination:<br /> Now, we know that some items destroyed in the Material World can end up &quot;appearing&quot; in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> But... Is that really true?<br /> <br /> Stuff in the Underworld are not really made of carbon and silicon... They are made of Corpus.<br /> <br /> And what is &quot;Corpus&quot;? It is some weird &quot;spiritual&quot; stuff.<br /> <br /> We also know that stuff in this plane of existence are highly affected by emotions... Memories, emotions, all of that shape the environment and even it's inhabitants.<br /> <br /> The Corpus of the Wraiths itself is highly dependant on their emotions - a Wraith that has no more passions simply ceases to be, their very &quot;Corpus&quot; dissipates into nothingness.<br /> <br /> Therefore, this is a Realm of pure emotion... It is an abstract Realm of thought.<br /> <br /> In that sense... It might not even be real! It could just be a &quot;theater of the mind&quot; for all we know. A sort of &quot;collective acid trip&quot;.<br /> <br /> But that's not the point. The point is that Wraiths may not be &quot;souls&quot;, but just simply a &quot;mental reflection&quot; of the deceased!<br /> <br /> This is a Realm that could copy the minds of those that died with far too strong will - so, if your will is too strong, it will &quot;imprint&quot; your mind into this Realm.<br /> <br /> But it is NOT &quot;you&quot;, but a mental copy of what you once were.<br /> <br /> There's actually some indication that this might be true. First of all, everything points out to there being a difference between &quot;soul&quot; and &quot;mind&quot;. Proof of that is that you actually need Spirit 5 in order to create a real human being, rather than just Mind 5.<br /> <br /> Secondly, there's indication that &quot;souls&quot; mostly don't carry over details of the &quot;mind&quot;, except for few fragments, with a few exceptions. How do we know this? Because Mage actually has reincarnation, and almost all of the time save very rare exceptions, you NEVER get details from &quot;past minds&quot; except for some disconnected flashes.<br /> <br /> Therefore, Mind (memory and emotions) is NOT the same as &quot;Soul&quot; (whatever that might be).<br /> <br /> The thing is thou, that Wraiths keep their full Minds upon their &quot;transition&quot;. They remain essentially the SAME as they &quot;were&quot; when alive, the same memories, the same psychology, the same emotions (sure, colourful due to their environment).<br /> <br /> Reincarnated Mages on the other hand, are different persons from their previous lives (different memories, different experiences, different minds)<br /> <br /> That is a strong indication that Wraiths are the &quot;Mind&quot; of the dead, rather than their &quot;Soul&quot;.<br /> <br /> The other problem we have relate to &quot;Avatars&quot;.<br /> <br /> What is an Avatar you might ask?<br /> <br /> I have no freaking idea, but but there's a strong implication that &quot;Avatars&quot; have something to do with &quot;Souls&quot;, whatever a &quot;Soul&quot; is either.<br /> <br /> And while I might not know what a Wraith is... I'm sure as hell that they aren't Avatars (from Mage)<br /> <br /> Therefore, I believe that there's a strong possibility that Wraiths aren't really souls, but rather just &quot;psychic reflections&quot; of the living upon the dreadful Underworld... As in, this is a Realm that &quot;copy&quot; the minds of strong willed individuals.<br /> <br /> That would make Wraiths be something akin to the Chimeras from the Dreaming. The Spirits of the Dreaming, the Chimeras, they are &quot;born&quot; out of the dreams and imagination of the dreamers (or sleepers or just simply &quot;humans&quot;). Wraiths could then, be something similar</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, even from the perspective of the system of mage, that does not work. <br /> <br /> Wraith and necromancy is general is shaped by the sphere of spirit. <br /> <br /> And countless sources including mage refers to wraith as being the souls of the deceased. <br /> <br /> Which is backed up by necromancers being able to track down the soul of someone they saw dying to the shadowlands or other destination. <br /> <br /> <br /> As far as the metaphysical working of a soul toward memory, it seems souls do indeed generally carry their memories s<br /> Howether, just like someone who might become amnesiac, memories can be locked or lost. <br /> <br /> The amnesia of reincarnated souls is clearly more due to the process of reincarnation itself rather than from a fundamental property of the soul, as shown by past lives memories, or the fact that souls that aren't reincarnated but go to other realms than the shadowlands keeps their memories. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T13:08:35-07:00","id":1538778,"title":"","content":"I don't think you are right, but there's no problem using your post as a means to help people think through the setting. That might lead to some productive conversations for some people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1538688-could-wraiths-be-fake#post1538688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stuff in the Underworld are not really made of carbon and silicon... They are made of Corpus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically they are made of &quot;plasm&quot;. Corpus is the name of the subtle body of the wraith. Plasm is the &quot;matter&quot; of the underworld. <br /> <br /> We also know that there are plasmic being that don't have their origins in the Skinlands at all. The creatures in the Tempest seem to have originated directly from there. These include angelics, demonics, tindelhounds, ailerons, cerements, shroudrippers, the kraken, mourners, djinn, and other phantasies/deleriums/legendaries/wyrds. I would also add the shifting zones as phenomenon that do not depend on anything originating from the Skinlands.<br /> <br /> Plus we know that the Neverborn were never alive - they predated creation. So it is not a case that plasm depends on memory, prior thought, or emotion.<br /> <br /> If your theory is true, you'd need to somehow prove that these creatures somehow originated from the Skinlands and are some kind of residual thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1538688-could-wraiths-be-fake#post1538688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Therefore, this is a Realm of pure emotion... It is an abstract Realm of thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not categorize the underworld as a realm of pure emotion or abstract thought. The astral plane is the realm of abstract thought. The underworld isn't that. Yes, when a wraith loses their passions, their corpus dissipates. But that isn't any difference from someone saying in the real world, &quot;after his wife died, he lost his will to live&quot; about someone who was physically healthy but died.<br /> <br /> The reason Passions are important to wraith is that they are what keeps a soul attached to this world rather than moving on to what is next. The entire underworld is a transition point/stage between the physical world and whatever awaits the soul after it whether it is Transcendence or Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Most people don't become wraiths, they pass immediately beyond. Rather than a realm of emotion, I would describe the underworld as an existential realm that is based on the nature of being/existence and non-being/non-existence. The danger of the underworld is that not only have wraiths lost their physical being, but they might also lose their metaphysical being as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1538688-could-wraiths-be-fake#post1538688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that sense... It might not even be real!</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not real in a physical sense of course, but it's definitely real in a metaphysical sense. Entities from other realms are capable of entering it and returning home. Real world occultists describe a variety of &quot;subtle bodies&quot; that a person has in addition to their physical one. People in the World of Darkness can definitely have astral bodies as well as physical bodies, so there is no reason to think why they also don't have plasmic bodies as well. <br /> <br /> In fact when users of Phantasm &quot;pull&quot; a dreamer's &quot;soul&quot; into the underworld, they are likely just pulling out that living person's consciousness into a preexisting plasmic body. Furthermore, this plasmic body is different than a wraith's corpus because it can only be damaged by aggravated damage because their bodies are even more resilient and sturdy than a wraith's corpus. We would not expect this if this is merely a mental reflection. It does make sense if we think their subtle body is stronger because it is connected to a living person who by definition should not be across the Shroud and is empowered by its connection to life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1538688-could-wraiths-be-fake#post1538688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's not the point. The point is that Wraiths may not be &quot;souls&quot;, but just simply a &quot;mental reflection&quot; of the deceased!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a case can be made that drones might just be some kind of mental reflection, but actual wraiths definitely have volition and consciousness. They aren't just some reflection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1538688-could-wraiths-be-fake#post1538688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is thou, that Wraiths keep their full Minds upon their &quot;transition&quot;. They remain essentially the SAME as they &quot;were&quot; when alive, the same memories, the same psychology, the same emotions (sure, colourful due to their environment).</div> </div> </div> </div>As do people who astral project or people who are capable of entering the middle umbra. So that means nothing.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, it is not entirely true that wraiths have the same memories, psychology, emotions, etc. It's possible for wraiths to partial or full blown amnesia. Their Shadow is essentially their sub-conscious mind, but dramatically empowered. When wraiths enter catharsis, they certainly act very differently despite being the same person, but that's a difference in degree to what happens in the real world when people who are drunk or high, have dementia, or experience head trauma suddenly begin acting very different - &quot;they aren't themselves.&quot; If wraiths were merely memories of people, I don't think that wouldn't be possible. Likewise even without that a wraith is capable of change - resolving fetters, getting in touch with their eidolon, or transcending.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1538688-could-wraiths-be-fake#post1538688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, there's indication that &quot;souls&quot; mostly don't carry over details of the &quot;mind&quot;, except for few fragments, with a few exceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree with this. The details of a particular life are incidental to a soul, not definitive to the soul itself, because by definition they are temporal, not spiritual (which is eternal).<br /> <br /> I don't think the wraith's corpus is the &quot;soul&quot; either. The corpus is just one (of many) subtle bodies that a soul &quot;resides&quot; in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1538688-could-wraiths-be-fake#post1538688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Therefore, I believe that there's a strong possibility that Wraiths aren't really souls, but rather just &quot;psychic reflections&quot; of the living upon the dreadful Underworld... As in, this is a Realm that &quot;copy&quot; the minds of strong willed individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't believe this is true, this is theoretically testable. We'd have to have a situation where a person has reincarnated, or had a near-death experience (meaning they died, but was later resurrected by medicine or other means and continue to live afterwards), or did indeed physically died but somehow came back (like a vampire), but also has a wraith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T14:22:13-07:00","id":1538787,"title":"","content":"My longstanding thought on this is that Wraiths are the parts of the soul that are not ready to move on. We already know that wraiths are generally people who have a strong attachment to the world. I think the psyche is that part of the soul that is still holding on to the world. The shadow, meanwhile, is the part that would rather cease existing than continue onwards. These two are the only parts of the soul resisting the call of Transcendence.<br /> <br /> The majority of the soul, including the Avatar, are chilling out on the edge of Transcendence waiting for the psyche and shadow to get their act together. One way or another it will eventually move on, either when the wraith resolves everything and lets go or it gets eaten away by oblivion. Either way the soul moves on, the only question is whether the wraith is still a part of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T17:29:29-07:00","id":1538803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1538688-could-wraiths-be-fake?p=1538787#post1538787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My longstanding thought on this is that Wraiths are the parts of the soul that are not ready to move on. We already know that wraiths are generally people who have a strong attachment to the world. I think the psyche is that part of the soul that is still holding on to the world. The shadow, meanwhile, is the part that would rather cease existing than continue onwards. These two are the only parts of the soul resisting the call of Transcendence.<br /> <br /> The majority of the soul, including the Avatar, are chilling out on the edge of Transcendence waiting for the psyche and shadow to get their act together. One way or another it will eventually move on, either when the wraith resolves everything and lets go or it gets eaten away by oblivion. Either way the soul moves on, the only question is whether the wraith is still a part of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I wonder if Transcendence is the same as Ascension (or Golconda), and if this is the ultimate stage of &quot;Nirvana&quot; (from Buddhism alright), upon which you just go chill out with The One and your Oracle friends in the perfect existence and no longer reincarnates anymore or not.<br /> <br /> And, if taking a dump into Oblivion is just like taking a swing upon the River Stix on Greek Mythology, forgetting your old life and getting ready to reincarnate or if... It means obliteration.<br /> <br /> But the idea that the Avatar (and other parts) keep hanging on the Ether, waiting for the Psych and Shadow to settle their differences and get their shit together is interesting indeed. This idea gives credit to the Chakravanti, then this existence as a Wraith truly is a blight that gets the soul stuck in the karmic wheel, unable to &quot;fulfill his destiny&quot;.<br /> <br /> It also, once more, ignite the same old question &quot;is Oblivion evil&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T18:07:18-07:00","id":1538805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1538688-could-wraiths-be-fake?p=1538778#post1538778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically they are made of &quot;plasm&quot;. Corpus is the name of the subtle body of the wraith. Plasm is the &quot;matter&quot; of the underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes. True enough<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We also know that there are plasmic being that don't have their origins in the Skinlands at all. The creatures in the Tempest seem to have originated directly from there. These include angelics, demonics, tindelhounds, ailerons, cerements, shroudrippers, the kraken, mourners, djinn, and other phantasies/deleriums/legendaries/wyrds. I would also add the shifting zones as phenomenon that do not depend on anything originating from the Skinlands.<br /> <br /> Plus we know that the Neverborn were never alive - they predated creation. So it is not a case that plasm depends on memory, prior thought, or emotion. </div> </div> </div>In that sense, the Underworld have many similarities to the Dreaming. Yes, I thought about the Plasmics. They seem however to be similar to the Chimeras of the Dreaming, beings created by the &quot;collective unconscious&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Neverborn aren't very different from the Fae from Arcadia either.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your theory is true, you'd need to somehow prove that these creatures somehow originated from the Skinlands and are some kind of residual thought. </div> </div> </div>The creatures from the Tempest are eerily similar to those in the Dreaming. Djins, angelics, demons... All of those seem to come from dream and fantasy rather than... Well, rather than being some sort of entropic things.<br /> <br /> What's more, the Tempest and the Labyrinth are also highly psycho reactive, undoubtedly having a high degree of reaction towards individual and collective mental patterns - individually it shapes according to the perceptions of individual Wraiths, collectively the environment shapeshifts based on huge collective psychic emanations. We need only remember for example that the &quot;Tempest&quot; was not a 'tempest' at all at the beginning, but rather turned into it due to impact of massive emotional impact of souls crossing into the Underworld en masse and without proper guidance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would not categorize the underworld as a realm of pure emotion or abstract thought. The astral plane is the realm of abstract thought. The underworld isn't that. Yes, when a wraith loses their passions, their corpus dissipates. But that isn't any difference from someone saying in the real world, &quot;after his wife died, he lost his will to live&quot; about someone who was physically healthy but died. </div> </div> </div>A person can spend years in deep depression; while it does abbreviates life due to the suppression of the immune system, it is not the same as insta-death. That's more common for widows with a certain age because their age already has compromised their health, but young teens can live with acute depression for decades.<br /> <br /> And I wasn't trying to conflate the Underworld with the Astral Plane; yes, that's true, the Astral Plane is the realm of abstraction. Pure Abstraction.<br /> <br /> Pure clearly the Underworld have certain similarities with the Dreaming (not so much with the Astral Plane), where at least some parts of the &quot;Collective Unconscious&quot; manifests<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is not real in a physical sense of course, but it's definitely real in a metaphysical sense. Entities from other realms are capable of entering it and returning home. Real world occultists describe a variety of &quot;subtle bodies&quot; that a person has in addition to their physical one. People in the World of Darkness can definitely have astral bodies as well as physical bodies, so there is no reason to think why they also don't have plasmic bodies as well. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but we don't really know what &quot;Astral Projection&quot; means. Maybe it's just an acid trip. Maybe it's all just in the mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact when users of Phantasm &quot;pull&quot; a dreamer's &quot;soul&quot; into the underworld, they are likely just pulling out that living person's consciousness into a preexisting plasmic body. Furthermore, this plasmic body is different than a wraith's corpus because it can only be damaged by aggravated damage because their bodies are even more resilient and sturdy than a wraith's corpus. We would not expect this if this is merely a mental reflection. It does make sense if we think their subtle body is stronger because it is connected to a living person who by definition should not be across the Shroud and is empowered by its connection to life. </div> </div> </div>Or maybe the mind of a truly living (and &quot;real&quot;) person is more resistant to the psychic blow than the make belief &quot;corpus&quot; of wraiths.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think a case can be made that drones might just be some kind of mental reflection, but actual wraiths definitely have volition and consciousness. They aren't just some reflection. </div> </div> </div>I know. I'm just trying to play Devil's advocate here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Furthermore, it is not entirely true that wraiths have the same memories, psychology, emotions, etc. It's possible for wraiths to partial or full blown amnesia. Their Shadow is essentially their sub-conscious mind, but dramatically empowered. When wraiths enter catharsis, they certainly act very differently despite being the same person, but that's a difference in degree to what happens in the real world when people who are drunk or high, have dementia, or experience head trauma suddenly begin acting very different - &quot;they aren't themselves.&quot; If wraiths were merely memories of people, I don't think that wouldn't be possible. Likewise even without that a wraith is capable of change - resolving fetters, getting in touch with their eidolon, or transcending.[/quote]<br /> Yeah, the fact that they are self conscious is probably the biggest indicator that they are indeed &quot;souls&quot;, yes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T07:57:24-07:00","id":1538839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1538688-could-wraiths-be-fake?p=1538803#post1538803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. I wonder if Transcendence is the same as Ascension (or Golconda), and if this is the ultimate stage of &quot;Nirvana&quot; (from Buddhism alright), upon which you just go chill out with The One and your Oracle friends in the perfect existence and no longer reincarnates anymore or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly possible, though I don't think it is in most cases. I'm also not at all sure that Ascension is the only &quot;final&quot; destination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, if taking a dump into Oblivion is just like taking a swing upon the River Stix on Greek Mythology, forgetting your old life and getting ready to reincarnate or if... It means obliteration. </div> </div> </div>I think its the river Lethe, not Styx, that takes away memory. But yes, I think it is a similar effect, though in this case Lethe comes as a sandblaster, not a gentle river.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the idea that the Avatar (and other parts) keep hanging on the Ether, waiting for the Psych and Shadow to settle their differences and get their shit together is interesting indeed. This idea gives credit to the Chakravanti, then this existence as a Wraith truly is a blight that gets the soul stuck in the karmic wheel, unable to &quot;fulfill his destiny&quot;. </div> </div> </div>It would mean they are at least right that destroying the wraith lets the soul move on. It is less clear that the soul moving on now is better than the soul moving on later when the wraith has resolved his issues.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T22:50:25-07:00","id":1538887,"title":"","content":"Wraith are... echoes of a person, and not the &quot;whole&quot; soul<br /> <br /> Parts of Being according the Egyptians (and many other cultures, but lets use the egyptians) - and this &quot;breakdown&quot; is actually present in every WoD game line not just Vampire or Mummy but not alwaays emphasized<br /> <b>Khat</b>, the Physical Body, was often preserved to allow a smooth resurrection - obviously a Wraith don't really have this. Unless they become a Risen/Kuei-jin<br /> <b>Ba</b>, the part of the soul that ventures into the Underworld - basically the Ba is a Wraith<br /> <b>Ka</b>, the part of the soul that remains close to the body and guards it from desecration - so we already have a &quot;missing part&quot;<br /> <b>Ab</b>, the Physical Heart, the seat of consciousness - see the Khat/body above<br /> <b>Khu</b>, the physical and mystical representation of a being - basically the Aura, that ties the spiritual and material parts together. Since Wraith don't really have a body (or had one untill it rotted away, turned to dust) this one is really weak to the point of almost nonexistant. Auspex 2 descirbes the Aura colour of a Wraith &quot;Weak, intermittent aura&quot;<br /> <b>Ren</b>, the True Name, a vital part of existence and the soul, a &quot;brief&quot; summary of what the person is<br /> <b>Khaibit</b>, the Shadow, which represent the darker urges and emotions of the soul - The Shadow of a Wraith (or the Beast of a Vampire, P'o of a Kuei-jin)<br /> <b>Sahu</b>, the indestructible part of the soul that will dwell in the fields of A'aru - The Eidolon of a Wraith technically (or the Hun of a Kuei-jin. tho' the Hun more like a bit of the Ka, since it lingers around the corpse, waiting to the P'o - the Hun could be the two combined)<br /> Between these parts flows <b>Sekhem</b>, the force of life itself that binds the other soul-parts together.<br /> <br /> Like the Wraiths themselves the Underworld is composed of memories<br /> For example the buildings and locations of the Shadowlands are memories of their Skinlands counterparts, and their appearance in the Shadowlands is a direct function of how they are remembered in the Skinlands - at least until enhanced using the materials of the underworld.<br /> <br /> Now the <b>Neverborn</b> present an interesting question (if you take Demon: the Fallen, it is answered, they are Charon and co who never been sealed away just dig themselves deeper in their forthress that eventually became the Labyrint) since they are never lived, never born...<br /> they represent beings who existed <i>before</i> the universe began or are themselves the shards of dead or husk universes, such as the Qlippoth. The cyclical creation, previous/failed universes are also present in Mage, Vampire (especially with Lilith) but even Werewolf - this is a bit reinforced by the fact in the Book of Madness Revised, at least some of the infernal entities served by the Nephandi are revealed to be manifestations or dreams of the slumbering Malfeans.<br /> With an interesting twist The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra suggests the &quot;Children of the Baali&quot; may be the Malfeans.<br /> These beings have physical bodies in self-created tombs in the earth, but their souls and minds exist in the Labyrinth, forever dreaming. The Baali seek to keep the Malfeans' consciousnesses from reuniting with their terrestrial bodies through sacrifices and depravity. If this lore were correct, it would suggest, as the Wraith corebook does, that the Malfeans are indeed physical manifestations of the pain of death itself (literally taking on the form of flesh and soul forever severed).<br /> <br /> Long stroy short: Wraiths are &quot;real&quot;<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T11:11:58-07:00","id":1538907,"title":"","content":"So, the Baali are truly the good guys that keep the world safe huh? That's what I call a plot twist.<br /> <br /> That does in a sense mean that they are not the entirety of what once was a &quot;person&quot;... Echos from the past... Chilling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}